Z||000005||recluse||08-22-2001||04:17 PM||||I have magnecor wires (i really like them), Split fire plugs, Fiero store cap and rotor, accell coil, I have not had any problems with it (yet) but i want to get rid of it, after trying accell wires I'll never buy another accell product.  I'd go with the MSD coil. I have a friend that worked at a GM dealership, most factory stuff is the best you're going to get, why do you think it costs so much? ||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||08-22-2001||07:10 PM||||<A HREF="http://www.magnecor.com/" TARGET=_blank>Magnecor</A><P>install everything Except the MSD box and see how it runs. Just installing fresh parts goes a long way. Don't buy the MSD box until you've seen how it drives for you after new coil, wires, cap, rotor, and plugs.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||2birds||08-22-2001||09:58 PM||||Taylor Spiro-Pro wires come in lots of colors.  I had the red ones for 7 years, no problems until found some chaffing on them. No more boot sleeves needed, either.  About $40 from Summit, I believe.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||johnt671||08-23-2001||06:34 PM||||I put an MSD blaster coil and box along with a K&N and 8mm wires on my 84.  Very happy with the mods.  Theve've been in since April with out any problems.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Mach10||08-23-2001||07:04 PM||||*raises hand*<BR>I've found that OEM replacement (solid 'trode) plugs give more consistant performance. I've got no faith in split-fires. Electricity doesn't really work like that...||||reg||7
